  "study_summary": {
    "objective": "Produce a first genome-wide RNA-seq view of the A. oryzae transcriptome (novel transcripts, UTRs, alternative splicing) and compare surface (solid) with liquid culture.",
    "experimental_design": "RIB40 was grown to mid-log phase (40 h, 30 °C) on CD agar-cellophane or in CD liquid medium, then exposed to 20 mM DTT (ER stress) or not, for 3 h or 2 h respectively; 2 replicates per condition.",
    "main_finding": "The transcriptome was far more complex than annotated (many novel transcripts, UTRs, upstream ORFs and alternative splicing), and genes/pathways possibly behind the higher protein production of solid versus liquid culture were identified."
  },
